\ locals.4 - named, per-invocation locals for RelF.
\
\ Why this exists: shell.4 currently has 181 global VARIABLEs, most of
\ which are not really global state at all - they are per-word scratch
\ cells, faked with a naming convention (GM-*, NORM-*, SCN-*, SAEK-*
\ and so on) because this kernel has no locals facility. That
\ convention costs real correctness, not just readability: a word whose
\ scratch state lives in fixed globals cannot be re-entered, which is
\ exactly why while/for/function bodies cannot contain another
\ multi-line construct, and why DO-WHILE's own condition/body buffers
\ cannot nest. See GOALS.md phase 8 and PROGRESS.md's Iteration 38
\ entry.
\
\ Design, in one line: a local is an ORDINARY VARIABLE whose value is
\ saved on entry to the declaring word and restored on exit.
\
\ That choice is deliberate and is what keeps this small. It means:
\   - No new dictionary machinery. Local names are just the VARIABLEs
\     that already exist, found by the ordinary FIND, so nothing has to
\     hook name resolution or splice temporary headers into the middle
\     of a definition being compiled.
\   - Existing code converts mechanically. A word's body is UNCHANGED -
\     `CA-SRC @` and `CA-N !` keep working exactly as before, because
\     a local still is a variable. Converting a word means adding one
\     {: ... :} line and deleting its argument-popping stores. The
\     VARIABLE declarations themselves stay where they are.
\   - The data stack and return stack are untouched, so this composes
\     with shell.4's existing, load-bearing >R/R> use (DO-IF,
\     RUN-FUNC-BODY) rather than competing with it.
\
\ The cost is that entry/exit copy N cells instead of moving a frame
\ pointer. For this codebase that is not worth optimizing away.
\
\ Syntax (Forth-2012's, minus the parts not needed here):
\
\   : COPY-ARGV ( src-argv src-argc --- )  {: CA-SRC CA-N :}
\     CA-N @ ARGC ! ...
\
\ Names before an optional | are initialized from the data stack, left
\ to right = deepest to top of stack, matching the stack comment's own
\ reading order. Names after the | are scratch: saved and restored the
\ same way, but zeroed rather than taking a stack argument.
\
\   : GLOB-MATCH ( pat plen text tlen --- f )
\     {: GM-PATTERN GM-PLEN GM-TEXT GM-TLEN | GM-P GM-S :}
\
\ Restrictions, all deliberate:
\   - The whole {: ... :} must be on one physical line. WORD does not
\     refill, and a multi-line construct here would be a close cousin
\     of the multi-line ( ) comment hazard documented in GOALS.md.
\   - Every name must already be a defined VARIABLE (or any word that
\     returns an address). An undefined name is diagnosed, not
\     silently accepted.
\   - LDECL-MAX names per definition, LSAVE-MAX cells of live
\     save-stack across all nested invocations. Both are checked.
\
\ EXIT and ; are wrapped below so the restore happens on EVERY exit
\ path, including the early `IF EXIT THEN` that shell.4 uses
\ pervasively. Both wrappers compile nothing at all when the
\ definition being compiled declared no locals, so every existing
\ definition compiles exactly as it did before.
\
\ This file forces DECIMAL for its own numeric literals and restores
\ the caller's BASE at the end. That is not boilerplate: tester.fr
\ leaves BASE at 16, and the first version of this file used a bare
\ `32 WORD` to parse names, which in hex is 0x32 = the character "2" -
\ so WORD delimited on "2" instead of on a space and swallowed whole
\ lines. Character constants below are written as [CHAR] rather than
\ as numbers for the same reason. See PROGRESS.md's Iteration 38 entry.

BASE @  DECIMAL

\ ------------------------------------------------------------------
\ Storing an execution token so it survives being saved into an image
\ ------------------------------------------------------------------
\ An xt is an absolute address, so a stored one is stale the moment a
\ saved image reloads at a different address - and, before that even
\ bites, it makes two builds of identical sources differ. Store the
\ offset from START instead and add START back on use. Defined here
\ rather than in shell.4 because both files need it and shell.4
\ already requires this one to be loaded first for {: itself.

: !XT ( xt addr --- )  SWAP START @ - SWAP ! ;
: @XT ( addr --- xt )  @ START @ + ;

\ ------------------------------------------------------------------
\ Forward declaration
\ ------------------------------------------------------------------
\ shell.4 is one linear definition order, and words genuinely need to
\ call each other in both directions - RUN-TOKENIZED and DO-IF,
\ EXPAND-BRACED-VAR and TRIM-PARAM, and a dozen more. Each has been
\ broken by hand: a VARIABLE holding an offset xt, a one-line caller
\ word, and a patch line after the real definition. Fourteen such
\ sites, three pieces of boilerplate each - and Iteration 76 ran
\ aground trying to add two more.
\
\     DEFER FOO          \ FOO is callable from here on
\     ...
\     : REAL-FOO ... ;
\     ' REAL-FOO IS FOO  \ patch it
\
\ The stored value is an OFFSET from START, not an address - it is
\ written into a saved image, and an absolute address there is stale
\ the moment it reloads. Calling an unpatched DEFER is a no-op rather
\ than a jump to address zero, so a forgotten patch shows up as
\ "nothing happened" instead of a segfault.

: DEFER ( "name" --- )
  CREATE 0 ,
  DOES> DUP @ 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN  @XT EXECUTE ;

: IS ( xt "name" --- )  ' >BODY !XT ;

\ ------------------------------------------------------------------
\ Runtime: the save stack
\ ------------------------------------------------------------------

4096 CONSTANT LSAVE-MAX
\ Raised from 256 in Iteration 90. Each nested shell construct
\ declares several locals, so 256 cells ran out around fifteen levels
\ of function recursion - shallower than shell.4's own
\ MAX-POS-PARAM-DEPTH of 32, which meant the SHELL's "recursion too
\ deep" diagnostic could never fire and the user got this file's
\ ABORT instead, killing the shell. A limit that pre-empts a
\ higher-level one is worse than a larger limit.
LSAVE-MAX CELLS BUFFER: LSAVE-STACK
VARIABLE LSAVE-SP

\ Each of these takes the slot as an OFFSET from START, not as an
\ absolute address, and adds START itself. That is what makes a
\ locals-using word survive being saved into an image and reloaded at
\ a different address (see save-system.4): the only thing compiled
\ into the word's body is the offset, which is position-independent,
\ exactly like kernel.4's BOOT hook and shell.4's deferred xts.
\
\ Doing the arithmetic HERE rather than in the generated code is not
\ just tidier, it is what keeps this free. The first attempt compiled
\ "LIT off | START | @ | + | call" inline instead, quadrupling the
\ code emitted per local - which overflowed the engine's dictionary
\ and corrupted compilation of shell.4. This version emits exactly
\ the same two cells the original absolute-address version did.

: LSAVE ( off --- )   \ push the slot's current value, so it can be
                      \ put back when this invocation ends
  LSAVE-SP @ LSAVE-MAX < 0= ABORT" locals: save stack overflow"
  START @ + @ LSAVE-STACK LSAVE-SP @ CELLS + !
  LSAVE-SP @ 1+ LSAVE-SP ! ;

: LRESTORE ( off --- )   \ pop the most recently saved value back
  LSAVE-SP @ 0 > 0= ABORT" locals: save stack underflow"
  LSAVE-SP @ 1- LSAVE-SP !
  LSAVE-STACK LSAVE-SP @ CELLS + @ SWAP START @ + ! ;

: LZERO ( off --- )   \ initial value of a post-| scratch local
  0 SWAP START @ + ! ;

: L! ( x off --- )    \ store a data-stack argument into a slot
  START @ + ! ;

\ ------------------------------------------------------------------
\ Compile time: the declaration currently being processed
\ ------------------------------------------------------------------

\ The xts of the four runtime words above, held as offsets rather than
\ compiled into L-COMPILE-ENTRY/L-COMPILE-RESTORES as absolute
\ literals via [']. Same reason as everything else here.
VARIABLE L-LSAVE-XT     ' LSAVE    L-LSAVE-XT    !XT
VARIABLE L-L!-XT        ' L!       L-L!-XT       !XT
VARIABLE L-LZERO-XT     ' LZERO    L-LZERO-XT    !XT
VARIABLE L-LRESTORE-XT  ' LRESTORE L-LRESTORE-XT !XT

16 CONSTANT LDECL-MAX
LDECL-MAX CELLS BUFFER: LDECL-ADDRS
VARIABLE LDECL-N      \ total names declared by the definition being compiled
VARIABLE LDECL-ARGS   \ how many of those take a data-stack argument

0 LDECL-N !
0 LDECL-ARGS !
0 LSAVE-SP !

: L-EMIT ( xt i --- )
  \ Compile "LDECL-ADDRS[i]  <call to xt>" - the one place any code is
  \ generated, shared by all four emit loops below.
  \
  \ The slot address is emitted as an OFFSET from START, with a
  \ "START @ +" compiled after it to rebuild the real address at run
  \ time, rather than as a plain absolute literal. That costs three
  \ extra operations per local per entry/exit and buys
  \ position-independence: a saved image (see save-system.4) reloads
  \ at a different address every run, and an absolute literal baked
  \ into a word's body is stale the moment it does. Found exactly that
  \ way - the first turnkey shell image segfaulted inside
  \ NORMALIZE-OPERATORS, the first locals-using word its startup path
  \ reached.
  \
  \ Two cells: the offset as a literal, then a relative call to the
  \ runtime word, which does the "+ START" itself. Both are
  \ position-independent.
  CELLS LDECL-ADDRS + @
  POSTPONE LITERAL COMPILE, ;

: L-COMPILE-ENTRY ( --- )
  \ Saves come first and cover every declared name; only then are the
  \ data-stack arguments consumed, in reverse (top of stack fills the
  \ rightmost pre-| name). Each loop is guarded by an explicit
  \ emptiness test rather than relying on DO with start = limit, which
  \ in this kernel runs the whole unsigned range instead of zero
  \ iterations - see PROGRESS.md's Iteration 15 entry.
  LDECL-N @ 0 > IF
    LDECL-N @ 0 DO L-LSAVE-XT @XT I L-EMIT LOOP
  THEN
  LDECL-ARGS @ 0 > IF
    LDECL-ARGS @ 0 DO L-L!-XT @XT LDECL-ARGS @ 1- I - L-EMIT LOOP
  THEN
  LDECL-N @ LDECL-ARGS @ > IF
    LDECL-N @ LDECL-ARGS @ DO L-LZERO-XT @XT I L-EMIT LOOP
  THEN ;

: L-COMPILE-RESTORES ( --- )
  \ Reverse of the save order, since the save stack is a stack.
  \ A no-op when nothing was declared, which is what makes the EXIT
  \ and ; wrappers below transparent to every ordinary definition.
  LDECL-N @ 0 > IF
    LDECL-N @ 0 DO L-LRESTORE-XT @XT LDECL-N @ 1- I - L-EMIT LOOP
  THEN ;

\ ------------------------------------------------------------------
\ Compile time: parsing {: ... | ... :}
\ ------------------------------------------------------------------

: L-END? ( c-addr --- f )   \ is this parsed word ":}" ?
  DUP C@ 2 <> IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 1+ C@ [CHAR] : = SWAP 2 + C@ [CHAR] } = AND ;

: L-BAR? ( c-addr --- f )   \ is this parsed word "|" ?
  DUP C@ 1 <> IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  1+ C@ [CHAR] | = ;

: L-ADD-NAME ( c-addr --- )
  LDECL-N @ LDECL-MAX < 0= ABORT" locals: too many locals"
  FIND 0= ABORT" locals: undefined local name"
  EXECUTE START @ -   \ a VARIABLE's xt yields its address; keep the
                      \ offset, so nothing absolute is ever recorded
  LDECL-ADDRS LDECL-N @ CELLS + !
  LDECL-N @ 1+ LDECL-N ! ;

: {: ( --- )
  0 LDECL-N !
  -1 LDECL-ARGS !                       \ -1 = no "|" seen yet
  BEGIN
    BL WORD
    DUP C@ 0= ABORT" locals: missing :} on this line"
    DUP L-END? 0=
  WHILE
    DUP L-BAR? IF
      DROP LDECL-N @ LDECL-ARGS !
    ELSE
      L-ADD-NAME
    THEN
  REPEAT
  DROP
  LDECL-ARGS @ -1 = IF LDECL-N @ LDECL-ARGS ! THEN
  L-COMPILE-ENTRY ; IMMEDIATE

\ ------------------------------------------------------------------
\ Wrapping EXIT and ; so restores happen on every exit path
\ ------------------------------------------------------------------
\ Both capture the previous definition first and defer to it, so this
\ adds behavior rather than reimplementing any of it. ; additionally
\ clears LDECL-N, which is what stops one definition's declaration
\ leaking into the next one - a definition with no {: therefore always
\ sees a count of zero and compiles no extra code whatsoever.

VARIABLE L-OLD-EXIT  ' EXIT L-OLD-EXIT !XT
VARIABLE L-OLD-SEMI  ' ;    L-OLD-SEMI !XT

: EXIT ( --- )
  L-COMPILE-RESTORES L-OLD-EXIT @XT COMPILE, ; IMMEDIATE

: ; ( --- )
  L-COMPILE-RESTORES 0 LDECL-N ! 0 LDECL-ARGS ! L-OLD-SEMI @XT EXECUTE ; IMMEDIATE

BASE !
